component SigilSourceIdentity {
  goal {
    Capture language-neutral source identity with snapdir walking and BLAKE3.
  }

  interface {
    SemanticInputs {
      Bind Implementation to only its captured path and exact bytes, fixed ontology
      and projection format, and frozen identity-catalog fingerprint. Selection and
      neighboring source changes do not invalidate that object. Design additionally
      binds the conservative transitive resolved import closure and required
      structural owners, frontend schema, language version, artifact version, and all
      structural relation arrays, and applicable config and glossary bytes including
      absence. Cycles terminate with a visited set. Unresolved imports conservatively
      bind the entire selected Design set. Recheck frontend source and context bytes
      against the filesystem before accepting that bundle as a current snapshot.
      Capture membership separately from the reusable per-source key. No production
      metadata enters either key.
    }

    SourceSelection {
      Select normalized workspace-relative paths and directories using Sigil include
      and exclude globs. Support arbitrary source extensions. Exclude generated
      internal trees and configured vendor directories. Refuse accidental empty
      selections and make intentional empty scope explicit. For explicit file-only
      selection, filter requested paths before hashing and do not traverse unrelated
      trees. Reuse snapdir file hashing and the same manifest encoding as directory
      discovery. Validate selected regular files and reject detected changes during
      hashing; no persistent shortcut replaces current content identity.
    }

    SourceIdentity {
      Use snapdir manifests and BLAKE3 content hashes. Hash a versioned encoding of
      sorted path, file type, and content checksum rows for selected scope. Capture
      exact bounded source bytes and compare their checksum with a fresh snapdir file
      hash. Reject paths crossing symlinks or workspace boundaries.
    }
  }

  constraints {

    StructuralBinding {
      Preparation and per-source Design binding include schema 2, languageVersion
      0.8.0, components and Facets, Tag introductions and groupings, import
      selections, bare references, links, ranges, and provenance. Changed relevant
      structure invalidates bindings through existing freshness checks even when
      semantic assertions appear unchanged.
    }
    SourceIdentity {
      Permission changes preserve semantic identity. Renames and duplicate-file
      additions change selected-scope identity. A file's identity depends on its own
      normalized path and bytes, never on neighboring source or model data. Disable
      snapdir symlink following and object-store checksum recovery. Reject explicitly
      selected symlinks and non-regular files.
    }
  }

  cases {
    FocusedSelection {
      Selecting four explicit files does not read an unrelated large or unreadable
      tree. Duplicate requested paths yield one manifest row. Internal, vendor,
      include and exclude rules still apply before content reads. Equivalent
      file-only and directory selections have equal identity.
    }

    SourceIdentity {
      Editing an imported file changes only that file's content row. The union
      identity changes, while the unchanged importer's source identity survives.
      Retained captured bytes do not change when the live file is edited later.
    }
  }
}
